      "text_raw": "Under phase W2, the second\nopamp is switched off and is\ntherefore left out. Capacitor\nC now finds itself between\nDC\nthe supply voltage V and\nDD\nground.\nCapacitor C now carries\nIN\ncharge V C . The total\nO IN\ncharge is therefore found, as\ngiven in this slide. If capaci-\ntors C and C are made\nDC IN\nequal, the DC output volt-\nage V ends up at half the\nO\nsupply voltage.\nThis sets the output and\ninput common-mode volt-\nages. All switches now have the full supply-voltage V as their V . This is also true for the\nDD GS\ninput switches.",
      "text": "Under phase W2, the second opamp is switched off and is therefore left out. Capacitor C now finds itself between DC the supply voltage V and DD ground. Capacitor C now carries IN charge V C . The total O IN charge is therefore found, as given in this slide. If capacitors C and C are made DC IN equal, the DC output voltage V ends up at half the O supply voltage. This sets the output and input common-mode voltages. All switches now have the full supply-voltage V as their V . This is also true for the DD GS input switches."
    }
